From: Nfrastack <code@nfrastack.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: stuck-at-bottom misdetected under tiling WMs / Ferdium

Bug: ScrollPanel.isAtBottom() treats the timeline as "at bottom" only
when scrollHeight - (scrollTop + clientHeight) <= 1px. Under Hyprland,
Ferdium (Electron) and fractional scaling the scroll position routinely
rests 2-9px off the true bottom while looking pinned (sub-pixel
rounding, custom themes, deferred layout). TimelinePanel then takes the
"user scrolled up" branch for every live message: it sets
canForwardPaginate and returns without rendering, so an open chat never
shows the newest message until something else forces a re-render.

Fix: widen the tolerance to 10px. Still small enough that a deliberate
scroll-up (dozens of px) is honoured, but absorbs rounding jitter from
WMs, wrappers and scaled displays.

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/structures/ScrollPanel.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/structures/ScrollPanel.tsx
index fc6ae11..36d0712 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/structures/ScrollPanel.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/structures/ScrollPanel.tsx
@@ -270,7 +270,13 @@ export default class ScrollPanel extends React.Component<IProps> {
         // actually lead to scrollTop+clientHeight being *larger* than
         // scrollHeight. (observed in element-desktop on Ubuntu 20.04)
         //
-        return sn.scrollHeight - (sn.scrollTop + sn.clientHeight) <= 1;
+        // NFRAPATCH: widened from 1px to 10px. Tiling WMs (Hyprland),
+        // Electron wrappers (Ferdium) and fractional scaling routinely leave
+        // the scroll 2-9px off the true bottom while looking pinned. With a
+        // 1px tolerance TimelinePanel thinks the user scrolled up and stops
+        // appending live messages until something forces a re-render.
+        //
+        return sn.scrollHeight - (sn.scrollTop + sn.clientHeight) <= 10;
     };
 
     // returns the vertical height in the given direction that can be removed from
